  "result": "Perfect! All 135 tests pass. Here's what I've implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Added VAT (Value Added Tax) calculation:**\n\n**New `lineVat` function:**\n- Calculates VAT per line on the amount **after discount**\n- Formula: `(lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 vatRate / 100`\n- Uses `roundCents()` for precision\n- Clamps result to 0 (no negative VAT)\n- Returns `ok(vatAmount)` or appropriate error\n\n**Updated `invoiceTotals` function:**\n- Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }` (added `vat` field)\n- `subtotal` = sum of line totals\n- `discount` = sum of line discounts\n- `vat` = sum of **rounded per-line VATs** (never a percentage of invoice total)\n- `total` = subtotal - discount + vat\n- Clamps total to 0 (never negative)\n\n**Key calculation order:**\n1. Line subtotal = qty \u00d7 unitPrice\n2. Line discount = line_subtotal \u00d7 discountPercent / 100\n3. Line amount after discount = line_subtotal - line_discount\n4. Line VAT = (amount after discount) \u00d7 vatRate / 100 (rounded per line)\n5. Invoice total = subtotal - discount + VAT\n\n**Updated `renderInvoiceText` function:**\n- Shows \"Subtotal:\" when discount or VAT present\n- Shows \"Discount:\" when discount > 0\n- Shows \"VAT:\" when VAT > 0\n- Shows \"Total:\" with final amount (always)\n- All amounts formatted with `formatEuros()`\n\n**Added 14 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- lineVat calculation on full amount\n- lineVat calculation after discount\n- lineVat with 0%, 9%, 21% rates\n- lineVat clamping to 0\n- invoiceTotals VAT calculation\n- VAT after discounts\n- Multiple lines with different VAT rates\n- VAT display in rendered invoices\n\nAll 135 tests pass \u2705",
